== Trivia ==
* A [[wikipedia:Straw man|"straw man"]] (sometimes written as strawman) is a form of argument and an informal fallacy of having the impression of refuting an argument, whereas the real subject of the argument was not addressed or refuted, but instead replaced with a false one. One who engages in this fallacy is said to be "attacking a straw man". [https://rationalwiki.org/wiki/Strawman_theory "Strawman theory"] can also refer to the [https://rationalwiki.org/wiki/Pseudolaw pseudolegal] concept of every individual having two personas — the flesh-and-blood person themselves and their "legal person" — with debts, liabilities, taxes, legal responsibilities, restraining orders, etc. only being applicable to the latter, allowing the former to (supposedly) flout laws that happen to inconvenience them. The fact that the Strawman item spawns a Keeper to be controlled concurrently with your original character lends credence to this latter interpretation of the term.
* Strawman, alongside {{I|Mom's Ring}}, is one of two items which cannot be rerolled into by {{I|Spindown Dice}}; in Strawman's case, this is because the next item by ID number is {{I|Dad's Note}}, which cannot be rerolled by any means (not even if rerolled into by Spindown Dice from {{I|Sausage}} outside of its designated room).

